        "content": "<p>I wrote a very small tactic (just a macro combining a custom-simpset and <code>by_cases</code>) that is aimed to help with junk values by introducing the condition and discharging the side goal with <code>simp</code>, see the examples below. The two questions I have are (a) do we want this in mathlib? (b) if yes, does anyone have a good name? (<code>by_cases!!</code>?)</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>Examples</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<p>Example 1:<br>\nbefore</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">condExpIndL1_smul'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SMulCommClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">condExpIndL1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">condExpIndL1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">by_cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">swap</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">condExpIndL1_of_not_measurableSet</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">smul_zero</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">by_cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hμs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">μ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">condExpIndL1_of_measure_eq_top</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hμs</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">smul_zero</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">condExpIndL1_of_measurableSet_of_measure_ne_top</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hμs</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">condExpIndL1Fin_smul'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hμs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>after:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">condExpIndL1_smul'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SMulCommClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class